1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,393
A media field stores the path of a file in the media library, not its address.

2
00:00:06,393 --> 00:00:11,145
In this video, you will turn those paths into URLs, resize images on

3
00:00:11,145 --> 00:00:17,180
demand, and render images and links with Liquid filters, Razor helpers, and tag helpers.

4
00:00:21,780 --> 00:00:24,980
A template turns that path into a public URL.

5
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:29,184
The URL is the media request path, with the URL prefix of the

6
00:00:29,184 --> 00:00:33,200
tenant and the CDN base URL added when the site uses them.

7
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:38,154
A resized URL adds commands to the query string, such as the width,

8
00:00:38,154 --> 00:00:40,342
the height, and the resize mode.

9
00:00:40,342 --> 00:00:44,948
The Media module resizes the image when the browser requests it, and keeps

10
00:00:44,948 --> 00:00:47,770
the result in a cache for the next request.

11
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:53,183
By default, the Media module signs the commands with a token that is

12
00:00:53,183 --> 00:00:54,884
unique to the tenant.

13
00:00:54,884 --> 00:00:58,476
Templates add the token for you, so any size works.

14
00:00:58,476 --> 00:01:02,320
A URL without a token only accepts the supported sizes.

15
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:10,110
The asset_url filter turns a path into a URL.

16
00:01:10,110 --> 00:01:15,249
The img_tag filter writes an img element from a URL, and each named

17
00:01:15,249 --> 00:01:17,783
argument becomes an attribute.

18
00:01:17,783 --> 00:01:24,470
An underscore in an argument name becomes a dash, so data_order is written as data-order.

19
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:29,040
The resize_url filter adds resize commands to a URL.

20
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:30,686
Name each argument:

21
00:01:30,686 --> 00:01:32,662
width, height, and mode.

22
00:01:32,662 --> 00:01:37,271
Without a mode, max fits the image inside the size and keeps its

23
00:01:37,271 --> 00:01:40,630
proportions, even when you pass only a width.

24
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:44,584
Crop fills the size and cuts what falls outside.

25
00:01:44,584 --> 00:01:49,568
Pad fits the image inside the size and fills the rest with a background color.

26
00:01:49,568 --> 00:01:52,950
Stretch fills the size and ignores the proportions.

27
00:01:53,700 --> 00:01:58,125
Set the pad color with bgcolor, as a hexadecimal value.

28
00:01:58,125 --> 00:02:01,461
Quality applies to JPEG and WebP images.

29
00:02:01,461 --> 00:02:07,119
Format accepts GIF, JPEG, PNG, and WebP, and without it, the image keeps

30
00:02:07,119 --> 00:02:09,730
the format of its source file.

31
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:15,037
When the field settings Allow media text and Allow anchors are on, the

32
00:02:15,037 --> 00:02:18,274
field stores a text and an anchor for each file.

33
00:02:18,274 --> 00:02:22,711
Use the text as the alt attribute, and pass the anchor to resize_url

34
00:02:22,711 --> 00:02:24,450
to center a crop on it.

35
00:02:28,667 --> 00:02:32,355
A media profile stores resize commands under a name.

36
00:02:32,355 --> 00:02:37,887
The Profiles page, under Media, lists the profiles of the site, with their hints.

37
00:02:38,356 --> 00:02:39,986
Let's open thumbnail.

38
00:02:39,986 --> 00:02:44,272
Its Width and Height are 160, its Resize Mode is Crop, and Format

39
00:02:44,272 --> 00:02:46,566
and Quality keep their defaults.

40
00:02:47,023 --> 00:02:50,108
A template refers to a profile by its name alone.

41
00:02:50,108 --> 00:02:54,651
The Liquid filters, the Razor helpers, and the tag helpers each accept that

42
00:02:54,651 --> 00:02:57,343
name, and the slides that follow show how.

43
00:02:58,943 --> 00:03:02,378
In Liquid, pass the name with the profile argument.

44
00:03:02,378 --> 00:03:08,043
Any other argument you name, such as mode, overrides the value that the profile defines.

45
00:03:12,243 --> 00:03:16,322
In a Razor view, the Orchard property gives you the helpers.

46
00:03:16,322 --> 00:03:20,895
AssetUrl maps a path to a URL, and IsImageFile checks the extension.

47
00:03:20,895 --> 00:03:25,591
The display template of the media field uses both to choose between an

48
00:03:25,591 --> 00:03:27,383
img element and a link.

49
00:03:28,133 --> 00:03:35,735
AssetUrl takes the resize options of the Liquid filter, and appendVersion, as named parameters:

50
00:03:35,735 --> 00:03:41,003
width, height, resizeMode, quality, format, anchor, and bgColor.

51
00:03:41,003 --> 00:03:43,939
Resize mode and format are enums:

52
00:03:43,939 --> 00:03:48,153
add a using for OrchardCore.Media.Core.Processing.

53
00:03:48,903 --> 00:03:54,886
For a media profile, call AssetProfileUrlAsync with the profile name, and await it.

54
00:03:54,886 --> 00:03:58,045
Optional parameters override the profile.

55
00:03:58,045 --> 00:04:02,683
Resizing applies when you pass a width, a height, or a profile.

56
00:04:06,883 --> 00:04:12,948
To use the tag helpers, reference the OrchardCore.Media package and register them in

57
00:04:12,948 --> 00:04:14,835
the view imports file.

58
00:04:14,835 --> 00:04:19,013
On an img element, asset-src sets src from a media path.

59
00:04:19,013 --> 00:04:21,573
On a link, asset-href sets href.

60
00:04:22,323 --> 00:04:29,610
The resize attributes are img-width, img-height, img-resize-mode, img-quality, and img-format.

61
00:04:29,610 --> 00:04:34,055
They apply when a width, a height, or a profile is set.

62
00:04:34,055 --> 00:04:38,063
For a pad, img-bgcolor sets the background color.

63
00:04:38,813 --> 00:04:43,753
Use img-profile for a media profile, and the other attributes override it.

64
00:04:43,753 --> 00:04:46,038
Pass an anchor with img-anchor.

65
00:04:46,038 --> 00:04:50,113
Add asp-append-version to put a hash of the file in the URL.

66
00:04:54,325 --> 00:04:59,319
This page shows one image five times, with different resize arguments.

67
00:04:59,319 --> 00:05:05,365
Under each image, the page prints the URL that the filter returned, without its token.

68
00:05:05,818 --> 00:05:07,604
Max keeps the proportions.

69
00:05:07,604 --> 00:05:09,167
Crop fills the square.

70
00:05:09,167 --> 00:05:14,748
Pad adds bars in the background color, and stretch squeezes the whole picture into the square.

71
00:05:15,212 --> 00:05:18,163
The last image uses the thumbnail profile.

72
00:05:18,163 --> 00:05:22,528
The other four ask for 200 pixels, which is not a supported size,

73
00:05:22,528 --> 00:05:26,032
and they work because the token signs the commands.

74
00:05:30,232 --> 00:05:34,288
Each syntax can append a version, a hash of the source file:

75
00:05:34,288 --> 00:05:39,511
the append_version filter, the appendVersion parameter, and asp-append-version.

76
00:05:39,511 --> 00:05:43,997
When the file is replaced, the URL changes, and so does the resized

77
00:05:43,997 --> 00:05:45,472
file in the cache.

78
00:05:46,222 --> 00:05:52,345
To resize with another library, implement I Image Processing Engine, and replace its registration.

79
00:05:52,345 --> 00:05:57,586
The Media module validates the request first, so the engine receives typed commands

80
00:05:57,586 --> 00:05:59,882
and never reads the query string.

81
00:06:01,882 --> 00:06:04,052
That's media in templates:

82
00:06:04,052 --> 00:06:09,476
asset URLs for paths, signed resize URLs for images, and profiles by name,

83
00:06:09,476 --> 00:06:12,189
in Liquid, Razor, and tag helpers.

84
00:06:12,189 --> 00:06:13,952
Thanks for watching.

